ondary Respiratory Symptoms: airway dilation is more likely primary to respiratory system, not cardiac", "Recurrent Infections of Unknown Origin: insufficient evidence to prioritize over structural pulmonary pathology", "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia Syndrome: possible but lacks direct evidence (e.g., situs inversus, sinus disease severity)"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic multisystem respiratory involvement (sinuses + lungs)", "Persistent airway dilation (objective imaging finding)", "Growth parameters in 25th percentile since birth (suggests developmental/metabolic concern)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Genetic Disorders with Respiratory and Cardiac Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.6116504854368933, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic onset since birth weakly supports structural/developmental causes rather than acquired inflammatory/immunologic processes."], "evidence_against": ["Airway dilation is more characteristic of structural/developmental issues than autoimmune processes, slightly weakening B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Inflammatory or Autoimmune Lung Conditions", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.121, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of classic cystic fibrosis features (e.g., situs inversus) weakly reduces the likelihood of a genetic disorder."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Immunodeficiency Syndromes with Recurrent Infections", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.109, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B4": {"